Diagnostic: fling coast-distance tracing (WEBKIT_FLINGVEL_LOG=1, off by default).

Follow-up to webkit-flingvel-log-diagnostic.patch, which measured the fling's
INITIAL VELOCITY and found it is not what varies: franceinfo.fr (heavy, user
reports slow scrolling) and a trivial local page both estimate ~4400 px/s for
the same scripted flick. The main-thread-load hypothesis that motivated the
first patch was measured on device and refuted - with the WebProcess main
thread starved to 6.5fps, velocity was unchanged and the UIProcess wheel
coalescer never engaged, because async scrolling acks wheel events on the
scrolling thread independently of the main thread.

So the variable is downstream of the velocity estimate. This logs what the user
actually perceives when the fling ends: the distance it really coasted against
the distance the model predicts (velocity/friction), plus duration and serviced
tick count. That separates three different failures which feel similar:

  - ratio ~1.0, many ticks        -> fling is correct; complaint is elsewhere
  - ratio << 1.0                  -> fling is being CUT SHORT mid-flight
  - ratio ~1.0, very few ticks    -> fling coasted correctly but was rendered
                                     too rarely to look smooth (a paint problem
                                     wearing a momentum problem's clothes)

TEMPORARY - remove with the patch it extends. Must apply AFTER
webkit-flingvel-log-diagnostic.patch (shares flingVelLogEnabled()).

diff -ruN a/Source/WebCore/platform/ScrollAnimationKinetic.cpp b/Source/WebCore/platform/ScrollAnimationKinetic.cpp
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/ScrollAnimationKinetic.cpp	2026-07-20 18:36:06.445990860 +0000
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/ScrollAnimationKinetic.cpp	2026-07-20 18:36:47.241239280 +0000
@@ -258,6 +258,7 @@
         m_verticalData = std::nullopt;
 
     m_currentOffset = initialOffset;
+    m_flingTickCount = 0;
     didStart(MonotonicTime::now());
     return true;
 }
@@ -274,6 +275,7 @@
 void ScrollAnimationKinetic::serviceAnimation(MonotonicTime currentTime)
 {
     auto elapsedTime = timeSinceStart(currentTime);
+    ++m_flingTickCount;
 
     if (m_horizontalData && !m_horizontalData.value().animateScroll(elapsedTime))
         m_horizontalData = std::nullopt;
@@ -286,8 +288,26 @@
     m_currentOffset = FloatPoint(x, y);
     m_client.scrollAnimationDidUpdate(*this, m_currentOffset);
 
-    if (!m_horizontalData && !m_verticalData)
+    if (!m_horizontalData && !m_verticalData) {
+        if (flingVelLogEnabled()) {
+            // The user-facing quantity: how far the fling actually coasted, against
+            // the distance the model predicts (velocity/friction). A ratio well under
+            // 1.0 means the fling was cut short rather than decaying naturally - the
+            // difference between "momentum is weak" and "momentum is being killed".
+            // ticks/duration separate a short fling from a starved one: a fling that
+            // ran its full duration on very few ticks coasted correctly but was
+            // rendered too rarely to look smooth.
+            double actual = m_currentOffset.y() - m_initialOffset.y();
+            double expected = -m_initialVelocity.height() / decelFrictionValue();
+            double durationMs = elapsedTime.milliseconds();
+            fprintf(stderr, "[flingvel] COAST actual=%.0fpx expected=%.0fpx ratio=%.2f "
+                "duration=%.0fms ticks=%u v0=%.0f px/s friction=%.2f\n",
+                actual, expected, expected != 0 ? actual / expected : 0.0,
+                durationMs, m_flingTickCount, -m_initialVelocity.height(),
+                decelFrictionValue());
+        }
         didEnd();
+    }
 }
 
 String ScrollAnimationKinetic::debugDescription() const
diff -ruN a/Source/WebCore/platform/ScrollAnimationKinetic.h b/Source/WebCore/platform/ScrollAnimationKinetic.h
--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/ScrollAnimationKinetic.h	2026-07-20 18:36:25.780108576 +0000
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/ScrollAnimationKinetic.h	2026-07-20 18:36:38.138183835 +0000
@@ -86,6 +86,9 @@
     Vector<PlatformWheelEvent> m_scrollHistory;
     FloatPoint m_initialOffset;
     FloatSize m_initialVelocity;
+    // Diagnostic only (WEBKIT_FLINGVEL_LOG=1): ticks serviced in the current fling,
+    // to tell a short fling apart from one that ran fully but was rendered rarely.
+    unsigned m_flingTickCount { 0 };
 };
 
